# Project-level ignores. The repository root carries the generic Python
# template (caches, build artefacts, .venv); this file covers what is specific
# to the experiment.

# Input data. data/ is normally a directory junction to the dataset folder
# outside the repository, and git follows a junction like an ordinary
# directory, so every file under it is excluded regardless of extension:
# the exports are ~11 MB each and are frozen inputs, not source. The directory
# itself is not tracked either: you create it as a junction or a plain folder
# and drop the exports in, as described in README.
data/*

# Untouched Open-Meteo exports with the wind speed, read by the configs that
# relabel the target (source: raw). Frozen inputs, like data/.
data_raw/*

# Generated results. run.py rewrites predictions from the config grid and the
# tables are derived from them, so neither is source. The directories stay in
# the tree because README documents them as the output layout. Every
# experiment besides the dashboard grid writes to a folder of its own.
results/predictions/*
results/tables/*
results/archive_wavelet_centered/
results/ablation_blh/
results/balanced/
results/horizons/
results/quantile/
results/transfer/
!results/predictions/.gitkeep
!results/tables/.gitkeep

# Local environment. Pipfile and Pipfile.lock ARE committed: the lock is what
# makes the run reproducible on another machine.
.venv/
.env

# Editors and Windows shell noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
